{"id":27782,"slug":"summer-interlude","title":"Summer Interlude","year":1951,"country":"Sweden","duration":96,"spine":613,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/27782-summer-interlude","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/72cf985f10f7c3fb55891726de421b92/6SmQWtN7jh7aMw3ZArD3H1Wj63sv2b_large.jpg","description":"\nTouching on many of the themes that would define the rest of his career—isolation, performance, the inescapability of the past— Ingmar Bergman’s tenth film was a gentle drift toward true mastery. Maj-Britt Nilsson beguiles as an accomplished ballet dancer haunted by her tragic youthful affair with a shy, handsome student (Birger Malmsten). Her memories of the sunny, rocky shores of Stockholm’s outer archipelago mingle with scenes from her gloomy present at the theater where she performs. A film that the director considered a creative turning point, Summer Interlude is a reverie about life and death that unites Bergman’s love of theater and cinema.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Maj-Britt Nilsson","role":"Marie","slug":"maj-britt-nilsson"},{"actor":"Birger Malmsten","role":"Henrik","slug":"birger-malmsten"},{"actor":"Alf Kjellin","role":"David Nyström","slug":"alf-kjellin"},{"actor":"Annalisa Ericson","role":"Kaj","slug":"annalisa-ericson"},{"actor":"Georg Funkquist","role":"Uncle Erland","slug":"georg-funkquist"},{"actor":"Stig Olin","role":"Ballet master","slug":"stig-olin"},{"actor":"Mimi Pollak","role":"Henrik’s aunt","slug":"mimi-pollak"},{"actor":"Renée Björling","role":"Aunt Elisabeth","slug":"renee-bjorling"},{"actor":"Gunnar Olsson","role":"Pastor","slug":"gunnar-olsson"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Allan Ekelund","slug":null},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Herbert Grevenius","slug":null},{"role":"